       pgmtopgm - copy PGM image


SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ppggmmttooppggmm


DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppggmmttooppggmm simply copies a PGM image from Standard Input to Standard Out‐
       put.  This may seem an unnecessary duplication  of  ccaatt,  but  remember
       that a PGM program can read a PBM image as if it were PGM.  So ppggmmttooppggmm
       can read either a PBM or PGM image and produce a PGM image as output.

       Even that is of limited usefulness because of the fact that almost  any
       program to which you would feed the resulting PGM image could also just
       take the original image directly.  However, sometimes you really need a
       true PGM image.

       When  you know you have a PBM image and want a PGM image, ppbbmmttooppggmm is a
       more general way to do that conversion.



OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       There are no command line options defined  specifically  for  ppggmmttooppggmm,
       but it recognizes the options common to all programs based on libnetpbm
       (See
        Common Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ .)


